\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces One uplink TB in one 180\nonbreakingspace ms release period. Until the 45\nonbreakingspace ms NeuralRx\xspace  deadline, the TB has a pending conventional recovery that no GPU queue contains. A failed, late, or missing NeuralRx\xspace  outcome requires one cuPHY recovery that ends before the guard.}}{3}{figure.caption.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:airan-background}{{1}{3}{One uplink TB in one 180~ms release period. Until the 45~ms \NRx deadline, the TB has a pending conventional recovery that no GPU queue contains. A failed, late, or missing \NRx outcome requires one cuPHY recovery that ends before the guard}{figure.caption.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Uncertain recovery need across channels and failure rates. (a) Share of TBs that NeuralRx\xspace  (solid) and the conventional receiver (dashed) decode in three channel models; each SNR is shifted so that the conventional receiver decodes half of the TBs at 0\nonbreakingspace dB. (b) Probability that a period with four admitted TBs requires at least $k$ recoveries when each TB fails with probability $p$. Lines assume independent failures; the band raises the correlation of the all-four event to 0.3. Circles are deployment periods that join the transition-SNR TBs of two consecutive measured periods; squares group four consecutive receiver trials.}}{3}{figure.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:debt}{{2}{3}{Uncertain recovery need across channels and failure rates. (a) Share of TBs that \NRx (solid) and the conventional receiver (dashed) decode in three channel models; each SNR is shifted so that the conventional receiver decodes half of the TBs at 0~dB. (b) Probability that a period with four admitted TBs requires at least $k$ recoveries when each TB fails with probability $p$. Lines assume independent failures; the band raises the correlation of the all-four event to 0.3. Circles are deployment periods that join the transition-SNR TBs of two consecutive measured periods; squares group four consecutive receiver trials}{figure.caption.4}{}}
